    {
      "body": "EVIDENCE. Reimage's plan-selection page presents one-year product plans, while the complaint says auto-renewal language was buried in a lengthy Terms of Use page and did not specify which packages renewed or the renewal charges.\nLEGAL REASONING. The legal problem is that annual recurring-payment terms were not clearly and conspicuously disclosed at the plan-selection point, before Paddle routed consumers into checkout.\nSTATED LAW. FTC Act Section 5(a), 15 U.S.C. 45(a); ROSCA Section 4(1), 15 U.S.C. 8403(1).",
